# kind | name | source (on-disk LICENSE path for shards; for clib/runtime, an
# SPDX id of licenses-spdx/, or the path of the library's own license file)
#
# Only what the released binary actually embeds: crest and the shards it
# brings, termisu, and not ameba, a mise tool that never ends up in it.
#
# The clib list follows the stdlib modules the tool requires:
#   Regex                      -> pcre2
#   YAML                       -> libyaml
#   HTTP::Client over TLS      -> openssl (libssl + libcrypto), through crest
#   Compress::Deflate/Gzip     -> zlib, required by the stdlib's HTTP
#   GC, static libc, runtime   -> boehm-gc, musl, libgcc
# CONFIRMED on 2026-11-18 against the static link line of this very binary,
# captured with `crystal build --static --release --no-debug --verbose` in the
# image crystalreleaser generates for its docker builds (alpine:3.24, Alpine's
# crystal 1.20.3), on linux/amd64 and on linux/arm64, identical:
#   cc _main.o3.o -o donico -rdynamic -static -L/usr/bin/../lib/crystal -lz
#      `pkg-config --libs libssl` `pkg-config --libs libcrypto`
#      -lyaml -lpcre2-8 -pthread -lpthread -lgc -lpthread -ldl
# (the two pkg-config calls give -lssl and -lcrypto; + musl and libgcc, which cc
# links without a flag). No gmp, no libevent. The libraries are the ones apk
# records in that image: openssl 3.5.9 Apache-2.0 (openssl-libs-static), zlib
# 1.4 Zlib, pcre2 10.49 BSD-3-Clause, yaml 0.2.5 MIT, musl 1.2.6 MIT, gc 8.2.12
# Boehm-GC, libgcc 15.2.0. This list is crystalreleaser's own. Re-run the check
# when a stdlib module or a shard is added or the image moves.
#
# The list is the one of the static Linux binaries, and a superset for the
# darwin ones, which embed the same notices. Those load libSystem, libiconv
# and the system's libz dynamically (otool -L of the release build,
# 2026-11-18), link Homebrew's OpenSSL 4 statically (static_libs of
# .crystalreleaser.yml; Apache-2.0 as well), and carry neither musl nor
# libgcc; their pcre2, libgc and libyaml are the ones the Crystal that mise
# installs embeds, at other versions (pcre2 10.42, gc 8.2.0, yaml 0.1.6 for
# Crystal 1.20.3, read from its embedded/lib/pkgconfig/*.pc on 2026-11-18),
# under the same licenses.
#
# MIT, BSD-3-Clause and zlib require the copyright notice to be reproduced,
# and their SPDX text only has a blank there: those four libraries embed their
# own license file, taken from their sources at the versions above:
#   pcre2    LICENCE.md  github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2  tag pcre2-10.49
#   libyaml  License     github.com/yaml/libyaml        tag 0.2.5
#   zlib     LICENSE     github.com/madler/zlib         tag v1.4
#   musl     COPYRIGHT   git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl    tag v1.2.6
# zlib.txt is crystalreleaser's own copy, checked identical on 2026-11-18 to
# the notice of /usr/include/zlib.h in the build image. OpenSSL 3 is
# Apache-2.0, whose SPDX text is complete as it is.
shard   | crest           | lib/crest/LICENSE
shard   | http_proxy      | lib/http_proxy/LICENSE
shard   | http-client-digest_auth | lib/http-client-digest_auth/LICENSE
shard   | cookie_jar      | lib/cookie_jar/LICENSE
shard   | termisu         | lib/termisu/LICENSE.txt
clib    | openssl         | Apache-2.0
clib    | pcre2           | licenses-upstream/pcre2.txt
clib    | libyaml         | licenses-upstream/libyaml.txt
clib    | zlib            | licenses-upstream/zlib.txt
clib    | boehm-gc        | Boehm-GC
clib    | musl            | licenses-upstream/musl.txt
clib    | libgcc          | GCC-runtime-exception
runtime | crystal         | Apache-2.0
project | donico          | LICENSE
